  "license_observation": "Exact upstream three-condition BSD-style LICENSE retained; no vendor SDK rights claimed.",
  "scope": "Supplied local log analysis only; no device access, CI fetch, external uploads or known-bad policy writes.",
  "changes": [
    "Canonical AgentBay-prefixed identity and explicit adaptation attribution.",
    "Entrypoint rewritten for supplied files and conservative evidence reporting.",
    "Remote-fetch guides/internal routes omitted; all required domain references bundled.",
    "Relative filenames prefixed to prevent awk treating names as options or assignments.",
    "Service helper rejects evidence windows that do not bracket the supplied failure time; restart alone does not prove crash.",
    "Service focus IDs and timestamp shapes validated; inverted or year-wrapping windows require separate slices.",
    "Passed individual/aggregate markers do not establish a complete successful run when logs may be incomplete or later failures exist. Missing-transceiver normalized gate requests a matching supplied service log.",
    "Final review: retain per-abort setup state and conditional uncertainty; fatal evidence takes precedence over retry wording without promoting ordinary vendor WARNs to terminal failures.",
    "Per-port fields reset at each test and dump/section boundary; latest snapshots identify their original header lines. Missing later fields never inherit an earlier healthy state.",
    "An available transceiver-info structure does not establish physical module presence; absent boolean evidence is reported as unknown. The entrypoint explains latest-test snapshot scope."
  ],
